(Node.js and Express) Tj T*
(Course summary | Instructor: John Smilga) Tj T*
T*
(A short summary of the course: how Node.js works, its modules and npm, and how to build a REST) Tj T*
(API with Express.) Tj T*
T*
(Week 1-2) Tj T*
(What is Node.js) Tj T*
(Node.js is a JavaScript runtime built on the V8 engine that runs outside the browser. It uses an event) Tj T*
(loop and non-blocking I/O, which suits servers handling many requests. Run a file with node) Tj T*
(app.js.) Tj T*
T*
(Modules) Tj T*
(CommonJS uses require\(\) and module.exports. ES modules use import and export \(set) Tj T*
("type": "module" in package.json\). Each file has its own scope.) Tj T*
T*
(Built-in Modules) Tj T*
(Node ships with modules such as fs \(files\), path, http, os and events. Prefer asynchronous file) Tj T*
(methods \(fs.promises\) in servers, and build paths with path.join.) Tj T*
T*
(NPM) Tj T*
(npm installs packages: npm init, then npm install name. Dependencies are listed in) Tj T*
(package.json and stored in node_modules. Use devDependencies for tools and npm run for) Tj T*
(scripts.) Tj T*
T*
(Week 3-4) Tj T*
(Routing) Tj T*
(Express maps an HTTP method and path to a handler: app.get\("/users", \(req, res\) =>) Tj T*
(res.json\(users\)\). Route parameters like /users/:id are read from req.params. Start with) Tj T*
(app.listen\(3000\).) Tj T*
T*
(Middleware) Tj T*
(Middleware are functions \(req, res, next\) that run in order. express.json\(\) parses JSON) Tj T*
(bodies. Call next\(\) to continue. Error handlers take four parameters: \(err, req, res, next\).) Tj T*
T*
(Building a REST API) Tj T*
(Model resources with HTTP verbs: GET reads, POST creates, PUT or PATCH updates and DELETE) Tj T*
(removes. Return clear status codes such as 200, 201, 400, 404 and 500, with JSON bodies.) Tj T*
T*
(Connecting a Database) Tj T*
(Use a driver or an ODM such as Mongoose for MongoDB. Keep the connection string in an) Tj T*
(environment variable \(process.env\) and never commit secrets. Use async / await and handle) Tj T*
(errors.) Tj T*
T*
(Quick reference) Tj T*
(require\("x"\)                          Load a module \(CommonJS\)) Tj T*
(app.use\(express.json\(\)\)               Parse JSON bodies) Tj T*
ET
